    "title": "When Does 'The Pitt' Season 2 Episode 9 Come Out? How and Where to Watch",
    "text": "Just when you think things can't possibly get any more chaotic in the emergency room at the Pittsburgh Trauma Medical Center, they had to go analog—aka, offline. With the line in the waiting room practically spilling into the street and staff searching for space in the hallways to handle the overflow as patients from other area hospitals impacted by a cyber attack continue to arrive at The Pitt, all while doctors scramble to reconstruct their assignment board and keep track of every single one of them without the help of their digital patient charts, we have a feeling its only heading downhill from here this week on The Pitt Season 2.Here's everything you need to know about tonight's new episode.When does The Pitt Season 2, Episode 9 come out?Season 2, Episode 9 of The Pitt is available to stream on HBO Max starting on Thursday, March 5 at 9:00 p.m. ET/6:00 p.m. PT.Related: 'The Pitt': What Is a Margarita Burn? Phytophotodermatitis, ExplainedWhat time does The Pitt Season 2, Episode 9 air tonight?New episodes of The Pitt drop every week on Thursdays at 9:00 p.m. ET/6:00 p.m. PT on HBO Max.What will happen in The Pitt Season 2, Episode 9 tonight?Dr. Robby (Noah Wyle) just might be toeing the line of breaking the law after suggesting a dose of pain medication for Roxie, the cancer patient on hospice care, that might cause her to stop breathing. If Dr. McKay (Fiona Dourif) goes through with the administration, Louie may not be our only code blue of the shift—and one promo photo appearing to show a bedside vigil for the patient seems to point in that direction.Dr. McKay sits at Roxie's bedside in what could be a bedside vigil. Photograph by Warrick Page/HBO Max(Photograph by Warrick Page/HBO Max)Plus, Dr. King's (Taylor Dearden) sister, Becca (Tal Anderson) arrives after complaining about a stomachache earlier in the day, but with Mel about to be dragged into her deposition, she may not even know the status of her sister. Based on a brief glimpse at the newly constructed whiteboard full of assignments, it seems Dr. Langdon (Patrick Ball) may just swoop in to save the day. After learning from the best last season, when Mel assisted him in breaking through to an autistic patient with an ankle injury, hopefully, his bedside manner has improved a bit.Related: Baby Jane Doe's Mother Details 'The Truth' Behind 'The Pitt's Emotional Lullaby SceneWhat is The Pitt Season 2 release schedule?Here is the release schedule for the rest of The Pitt Season 2.Episode 9: March 5Episode 10: March 12Episode 11: March 19Episode 12: March 26Episode 13: April 2Episode 14: April 9Episode 15: April 16Related: 'The Pitt' Actor's Behind-the-Scenes Look at Character's 'Gnarly Injury' Stuns Fans: 'That Took 2 Weeks?'This story was originally published by Parade on Mar 5, 2026, where it first appeared in the TV section. Add Parade as a Preferred Source by clicking here.",
